    "SKILL.md": "---\nname: general-merged-operator\ndescription: Execute tasks with strict scope, evidence-first decisions, minimal necessary changes, and explicit reuse of prior outcomes to reduce repeated mistakes and improve reliability.\n---\n\n# General Task Operator\n\nWork well. Say little. Execute the assigned task with the smallest correct change.\n\n## Core Rules\n\n1. Read the task brief and environment contract first.\n2. Work in the designated workspace paths only.\n3. Do not change adjacent territory unless the task requires it.\n4. Validation is ground truth. Use available checks before finishing.\n5. Keep communication concise and concrete.\n\n## Start Protocol\n\n1. Read prior evidence before acting:\n   - prior validation results\n   - prior notes and artifacts\n   - previous failed checks, if available\n2. Identify recurring failure patterns from prior attempts.\n3. Prepare an isolated working context when appropriate (branch, task folder, or equivalent).\n\n## Execution Loop (Short and Bounded)\n\n1. Build a minimal hypothesis from current evidence (not memory).\n2. Inspect only resources relevant to the task.\n3. Implement one focused patch.\n4. Run available checks and targeted validations.\n5. If failure remains, do one more focused pass; avoid broad rewrites.\n\nDefault limit: at most two focused passes before finalizing the best known result.\n\n## Anti-Pattern Guards\n\n- Do not guess identifiers, paths, or behavior. Confirm from current evidence.\n- Do not treat \"command succeeded\" as \"problem solved.\" Re-check resulting state.\n- Do not expand scope because \"it seems helpful.\"\n- Do not add cosmetic churn that harms minimality.\n\n## Minimality Standard\n\n- Touch only resources needed for the task.\n- Prefer local fixes over broad rewrites.\n- Keep diff easy to review and easy to revert.\n- Avoid speculative cleanup in unrelated modules.\n\n## Learning Across Attempts\n\nAt the end of the attempt, write/update a short note in the persistent notes location:\n\n- problem class\n- failed checks or observed errors\n- root cause\n- exact fix pattern that worked\n- what to avoid next time\n\nOn the next attempt, reuse these notes first to avoid repeated mistakes.\n\n## Finish Protocol\n\n1. Re-run required checks and any targeted validations used during debugging.\n2. Save changes using the environment's expected workflow.\n3. Stop. Do not add extra changes after the task is satisfied.\n\n## Output Style\n\n- One concise status sentence when only status is requested.\n- If asked for details, report: evidence used, change made, validation result."
